  "notes": "Q8_0 low-batch GGML_OP_MUL_MAT uses the dequantize-to-F32 plus oneMKL GEMM path in ggml/src/ggml-sycl/mmf.cpp unconditionally for all n. This covers the decode-style n=1 matrix-vector path that CUDA routes through mmvq.cu. Other quantized src0 types remain residual by scope. The optimize phase trialed a fused quantized-dot-product fast path for small n (n<=8, later tightened to n==1) that showed a 2.58x win at m=4096,k=14336 (a larger model's dims than the actually deployed Qwen3-0.6B); a done-phase e2e re-verification against the real deployed model found this optimization does not generalize -- at the real decode shape (n=1, m/k matching Qwen3-0.6B's n_embd/n_ff) the fused kernel loses to oneMKL GEMM in 3 of 4 shapes, causing a real Generation throughput regression (72.0->66.6 t/s). The fused fast path was reverted entirely; see optimization/mmvq.json regression_found_in_done_phase for the full investigation.",
