    "meets_expectation": false,
    "notes": "The fused fast-path trial (speedup 2.58x at m=4096,k=14336) was REVERTED after done-phase e2e testing against the actually-deployed model (Qwen3-0.6B, n_embd=1024, n_ff=3072) showed it does not generalize: at real decode dims the fused kernel loses to oneMKL GEMM in 3 of 4 shapes (m=1024,k=1024: 23.34 vs 15.21us; m=1024,k=3072: 33.87 vs 25.57us; m=3072,k=1024: 50.49 vs 22.96us; only m=3072,k=3072 favors the fused kernel), causing a real e2e Generation regression (72.0->66.6 t/s). Reverted to the unconditional dequant+oneMKL-GEMM path (matching true baseline behavior for this kernel); real e2e with the revert plus the (independently-verified) getrows and flash-attn-vec optimizations measures Generation 77.6 t/s (+7.8% vs baseline, entirely from getrows/flash-attn-vec, not from this kernel) and Prompt 635.8-653.5 t/s. See optimization/mmvq.json regression_found_in_done_phase for the full investigation.",
